{"type":"standard","title":"Carrie Buck (politician)","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Carrie Buck (politician)</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q106686764","titles":{"canonical":"Carrie_Buck_(politician)","normalized":"Carrie Buck (politician)","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Carrie Buck (politician)</span></span>"},"pageid":67558716,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1365522508","tid":"f6f2831a-862b-11f1-9787-6d308d379b4b","timestamp":"2026-07-23T00:18:01Z","description":"American educator and politician","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrie_Buck_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrie_Buck_(politician)?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrie_Buck_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Carrie_Buck_(politician)"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrie_Buck_(politician)","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Carrie_Buck_(politician)","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carrie_Buck_(politician)?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Carrie_Buck_(politician)"}},"extract":"Carrie Ann Buck is an American educator and politician currently serving as a Republican member of the Nevada Senate. She represents the 5th district, which covers parts of Henderson and Paradise to the south of Las Vegas in Clark County. In early 2025, Buck announced her campaign for the U.S. House of Representatives to challenge incumbent Dina Titus in Nevada's 1st congressional district.","extract_html":"<p><b>Carrie Ann Buck</b> is an American educator and politician currently serving as a Republican member of the Nevada Senate. She represents the 5th district, which covers parts of Henderson and Paradise to the south of Las Vegas in Clark County. In early 2025, Buck announced her campaign for the U.S. House of Representatives to challenge incumbent Dina Titus in Nevada's 1st congressional district.</p>"}